course: dictionary
lesson: 4053
title: Generosity and its clues
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Generosity is a noun. It names a quality, or an act of giving freely. It means being happy to give money, time, help or things to others, more than anyone expects. «Thank you for your generosity» is said when someone gives you something they did not have to give.
explain: Generosity can also mean being kind and fair when you judge people. Writers say «generosity of spirit» when they mean a warm, open heart that gives people the benefit of the doubt. Look for clues in the words around it, such as gave, shared, helped or forgave.
explain: «Christians read the vineyard parable as showing that God's generosity is not earned, but many find it puzzling and its fairness is discussed.» The clues are "not earned" and "puzzling": the generosity is a gift given freely, and people argue about whether it seems fair. Swap your meaning in: "God's giving is not earned" still makes sense.
fact: Generosity is a noun: a quality, or an act, of giving freely.
fact: «Generosity» means being happy to give money, time, help or things to others, more than is expected.
fact: «Generosity of spirit» means being kind and fair when you judge people.
fact: Many faiths teach generosity. The Good Samaritan helps a stranger in need, and zakat in Islam is a duty to give to those in need.
fact: Generosity is close in meaning to kindness, but it often means giving more than people expect.
exercise: «Thank you for your generosity, you shared your lunch with me.» What is generosity here? | Losing your lunch box | Running very fast | *Being happy to give to others, more than expected | Being very tired after school
exercise: Grandad says, «It was an act of generosity to give his time to the school.» What is an act of generosity? | A kind of test in class | A rule that everyone must follow | Cleaning the floor | *An act of giving freely, more than is expected
exercise: Which phrase shows generosity of spirit? | Shouting at everyone who is late | Counting coins in a jar | Running a race | *Being kind and fair when you judge others
test: «He gave his spare time to help the younger children read.» What does this show about him? | *Generosity, because he gave his time more than expected | Anger | Laziness | Tiredness
test: Which word is closest in meaning to generosity? | *Kindness | Anger | Boredom | Carelessness
exam: Read: «Christians read the vineyard parable as showing that God's generosity is not earned.» What does "not earned" suggest? | God gives only to people who work hardest | People must pay God back | God never gives anything | *God gives freely, not because people deserved it
